#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2278 expect=violation domain=PC
#note "column-absent case: the dataset has no PCLLOQ column at all while a 'BQL' result is reported, so the bare empty(PCLLOQ) leaf is TRUE on every row (absent = all-missing, EC-43) -> fires. PCLLOQ is Expected in SENDIG PC, so its absence is exactly what this leaf is there to catch. Plan B phase 4d' deleted the not var_exists(PCLLOQ) disjunct that used to make absence a separate branch; the verdict is unchanged."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 nameOnly=PCSTRESC
dataset PC label="Pharmacokinetics Concentrations"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PCSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PCTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col PCSTRESC type=Char label="Standardized Result in Character Format"
col PCSPEC   type=Char label="Specimen Material Type"
---
STUDY01 | PC | STUDY01-001 | 1 | DRUGX | BQL | PLASMA
